{% set faqs = [
  ["What are agentic payments?", "Agentic payments are payments initiated, managed or executed by AI agents on behalf of people or businesses. Paid by Agent groups them into three transaction flows: agentic commerce, machine payments and agentic treasury."],
  ["What are machine payments?", "Machine payments are transactions in which AI agents pay APIs, models, tools, data or other digital services directly. They are often automated, real-time or pay-per-use and may use machine-native payment protocols such as x402 or MPP."],
  ["What is agentic treasury?", "Agentic treasury is the use of AI agents to execute business financial operations such as transfers, card payments, vendor payments and treasury workflows within defined permissions and policy controls."],
  ["What is agentic trust?", "Agentic trust is the identity, authorization and accountability infrastructure used to determine who an AI agent represents, what it is allowed to do and whether its actions can be accepted. This includes delegated authority, mandates and emerging authorization frameworks such as AP2."]
] %}

